(169866, 9501, 4648, '<td valign="top">You got that title right as well as the photo.  If anything would have liked the stem in a little sharper focus, but good as is.</td>', 'You got that title right as well as the photo.  If anything would have liked the stem in a little sharper focus, but good as is.', '2002-12-11 00:27:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(169871, 9463, 4648, '<td valign="top">I really like this but wish the slices had been in focus.  Almost makes my mouth water, and had the slices been sharp, I''d be drooling.  Just a thought and my personal opinion, though.</td>', 'I really like this but wish the slices had been in focus.  Almost makes my mouth water, and had the slices been sharp, I''d be drooling.  Just a thought and my personal opinion, though.', '2002-12-11 00:32:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(169877, 9485, 5475, '<td valign="top">You did a very good job with a tough lighting situation. There is no way to do this without the front window being too hot.  Your foreground lighting and details are very good.  I also like the black and white format.  Smellyfish1002 (JD Anderson)</td>', 'You did a very good job with a tough lighting situation. There is no way to do this without the front window being too hot.  Your foreground lighting and details are very good.  I also like the black and white format.  Smellyfish1002 (JD Anderson)', '2002-12-11 00:51:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(169878, 9469, 5475, '<td valign="top">You have some interesting colors, shapes, repeating patterns, etc.  This is a concept that works well, but it would be interesting to see it shot from a side angle as well.  Although it would be against the rules for this site, I would like this shot better without the treetops on the horizon, and no branches on the left and right. Maybe cropping it down to the horizon would be an option.  It would get rid of some distractions and zero in on the interesting components in the photo.   I really like the way the red stands out from the bluish gray tones of the rest of the image!  I know it would be though to do, but increased DOF to keep the handrails in focus would help, IMO.  Nice shot, good effort braving the cold!  JD</td>', 'You have some interesting colors, shapes, repeating patterns, etc.  This is a concept that works well, but it would be interesting to see it shot from a side angle as well.  Although it would be against the rules for this site, I would like this shot better without the treetops on the horizon, and no branches on the left and right. Maybe cropping it down to the horizon would be an option.  It would get rid of some distractions and zero in on the interesting components in the photo.   I really like the way the red stands out from the bluish gray tones of the rest of the image!  I know it would be though to do, but increased DOF to keep the handrails in focus would help, IMO.  Nice shot, good effort braving the cold!  JD', '2002-12-11 00:56:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(169880, 9567, 5475, '<td valign="top">This is a nice shot and reminds me of many winter sunsets from when I was growing up in Indiana (I left there when I was 18).  I would have cropped more of the foreground out of this photo, or adjusted levels to send the foreground and the silohette of the tree to black. You have some jpg artifacts in the grayish area of the sky, but thats near impossible to get rid of.  This tree would be interesting shot with the setting sun directly behind the tree as well.  Lots of neat things going on here! Good Luck, JD</td>', 'This is a nice shot and reminds me of many winter sunsets from when I was growing up in Indiana (I left there when I was 18).  I would have cropped more of the foreground out of this photo, or adjusted levels to send the foreground and the silohette of the tree to black. You have some jpg artifacts in the grayish area of the sky, but thats near impossible to get rid of.  This tree would be interesting shot with the setting sun directly behind the tree as well.  Lots of neat things going on here! Good Luck, JD', '2002-12-11 01:01:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(169883, 9553, 3280, '<td valign="top">Good use of negative space, seems just a bit over exposed.  DPz</td>', 'Good use of negative space, seems just a bit over exposed.  DPz', '2002-12-11 01:03:11.000000', NULL, 1),
