(171340, 9433, 2490, '<td valign="top">This is one of my four tens in this challenge.  I love these colors, and it''s not a low-light, so your phocus is phenomenal!  The only complaint I have is that there appears to be an airplane contrail in the clouds that messes them up a little.  Obviously not in your control, and it''s the only flaw there.  Good job!</td>', 'This is one of my four tens in this challenge.  I love these colors, and it''s not a low-light, so your phocus is phenomenal!  The only complaint I have is that there appears to be an airplane contrail in the clouds that messes them up a little.  Obviously not in your control, and it''s the only flaw there.  Good job!', '2002-12-12 21:00:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(171341, 9553, 2490, '<td valign="top">And Merry Kissmas to you, too.  The white IS just a little loud here, as far as the brightness.  Maybe a little darker gray would have helped, but you know how that is.<br/></td>', 'And Merry Kissmas to you, too.  The white IS just a little loud here, as far as the brightness.  Maybe a little darker gray would have helped, but you know how that is.', '2002-12-12 21:01:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(171343, 9546, 2490, '<td valign="top">This is an incredible shot, in my book.  This an excellent bw.  My only complaint are the antennas on the buildings, and they aren''t your fault; they just affect your image.  Good sky.  Did you use NeatImage to smooth that up a little, or is this "original"?  Either way, it''s great, and it''s one of only four tens for me in this challenge.</td>', 'This is an incredible shot, in my book.  This an excellent bw.  My only complaint are the antennas on the buildings, and they aren''t your fault; they just affect your image.  Good sky.  Did you use NeatImage to smooth that up a little, or is this "original"?  Either way, it''s great, and it''s one of only four tens for me in this challenge.', '2002-12-12 21:03:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(171344, 9578, 2490, '<td valign="top">This is very well done, obviously with a quality lens.  Even if you post processed it to get this, it is still very nice.</td>', 'This is very well done, obviously with a quality lens.  Even if you post processed it to get this, it is still very nice.', '2002-12-12 21:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(171345, 9315, 2490, '<td valign="top">I''m giving this a 9.  For some reason the BW shots this week are really good.  There is a little shadow in the background on the right that distracts me slightly, and the whites on the right are brighter than those on the left.  Probably lighting, but it unbalances it for me.  Good job.</td>', 'I''m giving this a 9.  For some reason the BW shots this week are really good.  There is a little shadow in the background on the right that distracts me slightly, and the whites on the right are brighter than those on the left.  Probably lighting, but it unbalances it for me.  Good job.', '2002-12-12 21:06:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(171347, 9482, 2490, '<td valign="top">Excellent color work.  This could be a tutorial on how to effectively include all the primary colors in an image, and the stopped motion is beautiful.  9</td>', 'Excellent color work.  This could be a tutorial on how to effectively include all the primary colors in an image, and the stopped motion is beautiful.  9', '2002-12-12 21:07:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(171348, 9495, 2490, '<td valign="top">It''s very hard to effectively put a bunch of Christmas lights on "film", but you did a very nice job.  Looks like you had a better than average subject, but it is still very nice.  Good use of the contrast tool to get rid of some unnecessary background features.</td>', 'It''s very hard to effectively put a bunch of Christmas lights on "film", but you did a very nice job.  Looks like you had a better than average subject, but it is still very nice.  Good use of the contrast tool to get rid of some unnecessary background features.', '2002-12-12 21:08:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(171349, 9452, 2490, '<td valign="top">I think the background is a little bright, but that''s just my taste.  I''ve given you a 9, because this is a very high quality image with good composition and basically good color and lighting.</td>', 'I think the background is a little bright, but that''s just my taste.  I''ve given you a 9, because this is a very high quality image with good composition and basically good color and lighting.', '2002-12-12 21:10:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(171351, 9473, 2490, '<td valign="top">Even though I know all these are Christmas colors, perhaps its the particular shade of green in the background and the highlights on the purple that clash.  I think this would have been improved with a light background and softer overall lighting.  I also can''t find a particular spot in the photo that really portrays sharp focus.  If you worked really hard at this and I''m being too hard on it, I apologize :-)</td>', 'Even though I know all these are Christmas colors, perhaps its the particular shade of green in the background and the highlights on the purple that clash.  I think this would have been improved with a light background and softer overall lighting.  I also can''t find a particular spot in the photo that really portrays sharp focus.  If you worked really hard at this and I''m being too hard on it, I apologize :-)', '2002-12-12 21:12:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(171352, 9402, 2490, '<td valign="top">This particular shade of green really seems contradictory to the yule idea.  You''ve gotten some nice effects here, but they don''t suit my personal photography fancy.  I can''t decide if you''re a person who always has trouble with the tree lights or if you don''t like Christmas in general.  This shot just conveys a little bit of sarcasm from the artist to me.  Is that what you intended?</td>', 'This particular shade of green really seems contradictory to the yule idea.  You''ve gotten some nice effects here, but they don''t suit my personal photography fancy.  I can''t decide if you''re a person who always has trouble with the tree lights or if you don''t like Christmas in general.  This shot just conveys a little bit of sarcasm from the artist to me.  Is that what you intended?', '2002-12-12 21:15:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(171353, 9503, 2490, '<td valign="top">Those resolutions from last year frustrate us all :-)  I think this shot could have had a lot more perspective if some different angles had been included.  I always try to think of how a commercial or a movie maker would portray things like this.  Never flat.  Always use some angles to pull the viewer''s eyes to where you want it.  A combination of vertical and horizontally adjusted angles can do a lot.  I think you meant to use the rule of thirds, but it would have been more effective if the lines at the floor and walls pulled the viewer''s eyes from the corners of the shot to the rule of thirds point.  As well, don''t ever let these jokers convince you that EVERYTHING has to use rule of thirds.  That''s bunk - it''s just a guideline.  Center it if you feel that''s strongest.  Good luck!</td>', 'Those resolutions from last year frustrate us all :-)  I think this shot could have had a lot more perspective if some different angles had been included.  I always try to think of how a commercial or a movie maker would portray things like this.  Never flat.  Always use some angles to pull the viewer''s eyes to where you want it.  A combination of vertical and horizontally adjusted angles can do a lot.  I think you meant to use the rule of thirds, but it would have been more effective if the lines at the floor and walls pulled the viewer''s eyes from the corners of the shot to the rule of thirds point.  As well, don''t ever let these jokers convince you that EVERYTHING has to use rule of thirds.  That''s bunk - it''s just a guideline.  Center it if you feel that''s strongest.  Good luck!', '2002-12-12 21:20:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(171354, 9506, 2490, '<td valign="top">The first time I saw this, I was pretty hard on it with my scoring, but it deserves better.  Excellent detail, and the snag in the middle is lighted really well.  I''m betting a lot of folks with the famous uncalibrated monitor are killing you on brightness, because it is a touch dark.  I suspect that a print of this would disappoint you because it would come out darker than you think it is.  Awesome composition, though!<br/>7</td>', 'The first time I saw this, I was pretty hard on it with my scoring, but it deserves better.  Excellent detail, and the snag in the middle is lighted really well.  I''m betting a lot of folks with the famous uncalibrated monitor are killing you on brightness, because it is a touch dark.  I suspect that a print of this would disappoint you because it would come out darker than you think it is.  Awesome composition, though!7', '2002-12-12 21:23:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(171355, 9447, 2490, '<td valign="top">Excellent portrait with great composition.  The detail is so accurate it intimidates me.  I know this is one of you guys out there with a really high quality lens, because it shows :-)  Those of us with older, lower quality lenses and CCDs can never compete with this! Nice photography!</td>', 'Excellent portrait with great composition.  The detail is so accurate it intimidates me.  I know this is one of you guys out there with a really high quality lens, because it shows :-)  Those of us with older, lower quality lenses and CCDs can never compete with this! Nice photography!', '2002-12-12 21:27:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(171356, 9583, 2490, '<td valign="top">I''m not a big abstract fan, but this is well done.  Great color.  I think I would like it even better without the little bits of yellow.</td>', 'I''m not a big abstract fan, but this is well done.  Great color.  I think I would like it even better without the little bits of yellow.', '2002-12-12 21:28:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(171357, 9521, 2490, '<td valign="top">I can''t explain why I like this, but I do.  Good shot.  His expression says a lot, but the "photo" in the background carries a huge air of mystery that keeps me staring at the shot.  9</td>', 'I can''t explain why I like this, but I do.  Good shot.  His expression says a lot, but the "photo" in the background carries a huge air of mystery that keeps me staring at the shot.  9', '2002-12-12 21:29:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(171392, 9558, 5475, '<td valign="top">Sorry, but not a lot going on here in my opinion.  I would have given a higher score if you had placed the object off center.  I am assuming this is the moon, but there isn''t enough detail to confirm that.   If it is the moon, that''s a whole lot of green cheese!</td>', 'Sorry, but not a lot going on here in my opinion.  I would have given a higher score if you had placed the object off center.  I am assuming this is the moon, but there isn''t enough detail to confirm that.   If it is the moon, that''s a whole lot of green cheese!', '2002-12-12 22:07:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(171394, 9383, 5475, '<td valign="top">Nice use of DOF.I would have liked to see a little more light on the mouthpiece.  Nice angle.. kind of an uncommon approach.  I like that.  JD</td>', 'Nice use of DOF.I would have liked to see a little more light on the mouthpiece.  Nice angle.. kind of an uncommon approach.  I like that.  JD', '2002-12-12 22:08:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(171419, 9561, 4162, '<td valign="top">I like the consistancy of colour and light throughout the whole picture.</td>', 'I like the consistancy of colour and light throughout the whole picture.', '2002-12-12 22:40:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(171420, 9463, 4162, '<td valign="top">Not sure that I like the use of DOF here, cause I think that the lemon at the back is more interesting than the lemon at the front and so want to see more of that one! Thats just me though!</td>', 'Not sure that I like the use of DOF here, cause I think that the lemon at the back is more interesting than the lemon at the front and so want to see more of that one! Thats just me though!', '2002-12-12 22:43:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(171421, 9386, 4493, '<td valign="top">Colors are good, focus is good. I think that for me there isn''t enough around it to give give it atmosphere, it just looks like a fire.</td>', 'Colors are good, focus is good. I think that for me there isn''t enough around it to give give it atmosphere, it just looks like a fire.', '2002-12-12 22:43:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(171425, 9551, 4162, '<td valign="top">Hope that my stairway to heaven is not as old and rusty as this one! Interesting picture though.  Maybe it could be a little more to the left, to even out the corners of the top of the frame.</td>', 'Hope that my stairway to heaven is not as old and rusty as this one! Interesting picture though.  Maybe it could be a little more to the left, to even out the corners of the top of the frame.', '2002-12-12 22:46:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(171426, 9585, 4493, '<td valign="top">Nice clear shot. Great focus. The lighting may be a little bright on the right. Not sure about the close-up crop. Doesn''t have any story to it for me.</td>', 'Nice clear shot. Great focus. The lighting may be a little bright on the right. Not sure about the close-up crop. Doesn''t have any story to it for me.', '2002-12-12 22:47:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(171427, 9575, 4162, '<td valign="top">Ha! Great picture! Lighting is a tiny bit harsh on the back of the snail .</td>', 'Ha! Great picture! Lighting is a tiny bit harsh on the back of the snail .', '2002-12-12 22:47:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(171430, 9315, 4162, '<td valign="top">Super sharp! I need to learn to use the sharpening tool, the effects here are great!</td>', 'Super sharp! I need to learn to use the sharpening tool, the effects here are great!', '2002-12-12 22:49:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(171432, 9559, 4162, '<td valign="top">A bit too grainy but interesting lines shown in the composition</td>', 'A bit too grainy but interesting lines shown in the composition', '2002-12-12 22:50:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(171435, 9522, 4493, '<td valign="top">Your capture of the white in the snow is good. It''s not blue or oversaturated. The detail in the trunk is crisp. The one drawback I see is that the  crop may be to tight. More trunk on the left would be nice.</td>', 'Your capture of the white in the snow is good. It''s not blue or oversaturated. The detail in the trunk is crisp. The one drawback I see is that the  crop may be to tight. More trunk on the left would be nice.', '2002-12-12 22:51:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(171436, 9510, 4162, '<td valign="top">Great focus and DOF here, lovely capture of the expression. Possibly a bit too much background space.</td>', 'Great focus and DOF here, lovely capture of the expression. Possibly a bit too much background space.', '2002-12-12 22:52:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(171438, 9582, 1037, '<td valign="top">This definitely has that "wow" factor everyone talks about :). The red ball against the pure white background is perfect. I love the yellow hot spot on it. I''m sure a lot of people will say the needles of the pine tree should all be in focus, but I love the DOF you''ve used! The overall effect has a subtle resemblance to a watercolour painting. It would be great on a Christmas card (I''m sure a lot of other people are saying that too!)</td>', 'This definitely has that "wow" factor everyone talks about :). The red ball against the pure white background is perfect. I love the yellow hot spot on it. I''m sure a lot of people will say the needles of the pine tree should all be in focus, but I love the DOF you''ve used! The overall effect has a subtle resemblance to a watercolour painting. It would be great on a Christmas card (I''m sure a lot of other people are saying that too!)', '2002-12-12 22:53:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(171441, 9568, 4493, '<td valign="top">Great capture of the moment. My feeling is that a crop to make this a portrait shot instead of landscape would have helped keep the eye over on the left where the action is. As it is now, I am drawn to the trees instead of the bird.</td>', 'Great capture of the moment. My feeling is that a crop to make this a portrait shot instead of landscape would have helped keep the eye over on the left where the action is. As it is now, I am drawn to the trees instead of the bird.', '2002-12-12 22:54:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(171442, 9417, 4162, '<td valign="top">Lovely portrait. I was expecting a Xmas bauble around his neck or something like that, cause of the title.</td>', 'Lovely portrait. I was expecting a Xmas bauble around his neck or something like that, cause of the title.', '2002-12-12 22:54:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(171443, 9494, 4493, '<td valign="top">Whites are oversaturated. The subject is interesting and the man''s body language and expression are interesting. Color may have also worked for this shot.</td>', 'Whites are oversaturated. The subject is interesting and the man''s body language and expression are interesting. Color may have also worked for this shot.', '2002-12-12 22:56:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(171445, 9519, 4493, '<td valign="top">Nice candid. Colors are good.</td>', 'Nice candid. Colors are good.', '2002-12-12 22:57:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(171447, 9465, 1037, '<td valign="top">I like this, but I think it would have worked a bit better with more space above her head. It''s the kind of subject that lends itself well to negative space, to create mystery and tension.<br/> <br/>Otherwise, this is technically good and an intriguing photo. I think perhaps the centred composition and symmetry makes it seem a bit too formal and static for this theme. Strong emotions are better represented in a spontaneous, less staged way, in my opinion. So, I guess my suggestion would be to take her off-centre, take a different camera angle, and leave more dark space in the area of the photo that her eyes lead you to look at. But leave everything else just the way it is (lighting, etc.) because it''s really good :).</td>', 'I like this, but I think it would have worked a bit better with more space above her head. It''s the kind of subject that lends itself well to negative space, to create mystery and tension. Otherwise, this is technically good and an intriguing photo. I think perhaps the centred composition and symmetry makes it seem a bit too formal and static for this theme. Strong emotions are better represented in a spontaneous, less staged way, in my opinion. So, I guess my suggestion would be to take her off-centre, take a different camera angle, and leave more dark space in the area of the photo that her eyes lead you to look at. But leave everything else just the way it is (lighting, etc.) because it''s really good :).', '2002-12-12 23:01:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(171449, 9568, 1037, '<td valign="top">I love the silhouettes here, of the angel statue against the delicate, beautiful bare trees and the bird. The positioning of the sun behind the statue is great. But something about the composition spoils it a little. I think all it needs is a slightly tighter crop, and it would be wonderful.<br/> <br/>The dark tones also seem slightly grey to me. Some levels adjustment would give it just that extra bit of depth and contrast to increase the impact of the silhouettes. Nice work otherwise.</td>', 'I love the silhouettes here, of the angel statue against the delicate, beautiful bare trees and the bird. The positioning of the sun behind the statue is great. But something about the composition spoils it a little. I think all it needs is a slightly tighter crop, and it would be wonderful. The dark tones also seem slightly grey to me. Some levels adjustment would give it just that extra bit of depth and contrast to increase the impact of the silhouettes. Nice work otherwise.', '2002-12-12 23:04:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(171451, 9369, 1037, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea and a technically strong study. The only thing that doesn''t work for me is the amount of shine at the base of the apple. It has an odd effect that draws my eye away from the holly on the top. The photo doesn''t grab me, but is objectively very good.</td>', 'Interesting idea and a technically strong study. The only thing that doesn''t work for me is the amount of shine at the base of the apple. It has an odd effect that draws my eye away from the holly on the top. The photo doesn''t grab me, but is objectively very good.', '2002-12-12 23:06:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(171454, 9469, 1037, '<td valign="top">Wow... something I''ll never see in real life unless I travel more :). I like this photo a lot. The composition is strong and the colours are very beautiful. I love all those blue and white tones. The DOF is a little bit distracting, but that''s only a minor point for me. It''s a really interesting scene.</td>', 'Wow... something I''ll never see in real life unless I travel more :). I like this photo a lot. The composition is strong and the colours are very beautiful. I love all those blue and white tones. The DOF is a little bit distracting, but that''s only a minor point for me. It''s a really interesting scene.', '2002-12-12 23:09:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(171461, 9436, 1037, '<td valign="top">Wow, cute!!! It looks like you have a low res camera or you cropped this a lot, but that doesn''t worry me. What an adorable, pink little nose :). The composition couldn''t be any better, the DOF works well to blur the tree trunk and draw your eyes to the squirrel. The snow in the background has just enough texture and colour variation to avoid being stark, but isn''t a distraction. Very good work :). I''m giving it 10 for pushing all the right buttons so well.</td>', 'Wow, cute!!! It looks like you have a low res camera or you cropped this a lot, but that doesn''t worry me. What an adorable, pink little nose :). The composition couldn''t be any better, the DOF works well to blur the tree trunk and draw your eyes to the squirrel. The snow in the background has just enough texture and colour variation to avoid being stark, but isn''t a distraction. Very good work :). I''m giving it 10 for pushing all the right buttons so well.', '2002-12-12 23:12:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(171472, 9526, 1037, '<td valign="top">There are some interesting shapes and textures in here, but I''m not sure what I''m looking at! What are these things? Maybe it''s a cultural barrier, because the  theme of this Free Study challenge has turned out to be northern hemisphere wintery photos, and I''m sitting here in my southern hemisphere summer clothes :).<br/> <br/>The composition is a little bit awkward, I''m not sure what is supposed to hold my attention. I keep going back to the older object, because I like the weathered paint on it, but the photo isn''t interesting to me overall.</td>', 'There are some interesting shapes and textures in here, but I''m not sure what I''m looking at! What are these things? Maybe it''s a cultural barrier, because the  theme of this Free Study challenge has turned out to be northern hemisphere wintery photos, and I''m sitting here in my southern hemisphere summer clothes :). The composition is a little bit awkward, I''m not sure what is supposed to hold my attention. I keep going back to the older object, because I like the weathered paint on it, but the photo isn''t interesting to me overall.', '2002-12-12 23:19:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(171476, 9439, 1037, '<td valign="top">This is a very atmospheric image. It definitely puts me in that early morning mood. I''m the kind of person who can be hypnotised by shadows on walls, especially when they''re as lovely as this. The colours here are beautiful and warm. I think I would have liked more of the chair to be in the photo, though. As it is, it draws my eyes out of the photo, looking for the rest of the chair. Nice work, otherwise.</td>', 'This is a very atmospheric image. It definitely puts me in that early morning mood. I''m the kind of person who can be hypnotised by shadows on walls, especially when they''re as lovely as this. The colours here are beautiful and warm. I think I would have liked more of the chair to be in the photo, though. As it is, it draws my eyes out of the photo, looking for the rest of the chair. Nice work, otherwise.', '2002-12-12 23:22:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(171479, 9383, 772, '<td valign="top">very nice composition and perspective on this photo... the shallow depth of field works very well here and it isolates the mouthpiece well.  The lighting is a bit strange, but i think that is what sets this photo apart... great shot :) - setzler</td>', 'very nice composition and perspective on this photo... the shallow depth of field works very well here and it isolates the mouthpiece well.  The lighting is a bit strange, but i think that is what sets this photo apart... great shot :) - setzler', '2002-12-12 23:24:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(171480, 9378, 1037, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous! I love the composition here, just ordered enough to work but just loose enough not to look too staged and static. The interplay of light and colour is beautiful. The DOF gives it some nice depth, and I especially like that there are little flecks of dust... perfection makes me feel uneasy. I''m giving it 10!</td>', 'Gorgeous! I love the composition here, just ordered enough to work but just loose enough not to look too staged and static. The interplay of light and colour is beautiful. The DOF gives it some nice depth, and I especially like that there are little flecks of dust... perfection makes me feel uneasy. I''m giving it 10!', '2002-12-12 23:24:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(171482, 9390, 772, '<td valign="top">excellent shot... I believe this could be the cover on a game box or a cd :)  Great work... - setzler</td>', 'excellent shot... I believe this could be the cover on a game box or a cd :)  Great work... - setzler', '2002-12-12 23:25:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(171487, 9503, 1037, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting black and white study. I like all the dirt and grime, and the texturing on the wall and floor. It''s an interesting commentary on our modern consumer society (if you want to get all cerebral about it :)). <br/> <br/>It lacks something though. The photo is overall a little bit too grey, and I think I would like the shadows to be slightly longer and stronger to life the exercise equpiment from its surroundings more. The composition seems a bit too formal and static... some strong diagonal lines would help it along. Nice work though.</td>', 'This is an interesting black and white study. I like all the dirt and grime, and the texturing on the wall and floor. It''s an interesting commentary on our modern consumer society (if you want to get all cerebral about it :)).  It lacks something though. The photo is overall a little bit too grey, and I think I would like the shadows to be slightly longer and stronger to life the exercise equpiment from its surroundings more. The composition seems a bit too formal and static... some strong diagonal lines would help it along. Nice work though.', '2002-12-12 23:27:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(171503, 9396, 1037, '<td valign="top">Cool idea. Reminds me a bit of one of Man Ray''s "rayograph" style photos, where he just place objects on the photographic paper under the enlarger (although, yours is what you would get if you toook a negative of that). Compsitionally, the thread works really well in providing a path for your eyes to take around the needles. It''s a great idea! Very experimental.</td>', 'Cool idea. Reminds me a bit of one of Man Ray''s "rayograph" style photos, where he just place objects on the photographic paper under the enlarger (although, yours is what you would get if you toook a negative of that). Compsitionally, the thread works really well in providing a path for your eyes to take around the needles. It''s a great idea! Very experimental.', '2002-12-12 23:34:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(171510, 9402, 1037, '<td valign="top">Hehe, I recognise this :). The lights don''t quite create the same kind of impression the barbed wire did, but it works on a completely different level. Kind of surreal in a humorous way (a bit Dada?). The effect of the coloured lights against the skin is gorgeous, turning it mostly green like some kind of forest sprite. I love the shadows on the neck.<br/> <br/>Just... interesting and weird. I love it!</td>', 'Hehe, I recognise this :). The lights don''t quite create the same kind of impression the barbed wire did, but it works on a completely different level. Kind of surreal in a humorous way (a bit Dada?). The effect of the coloured lights against the skin is gorgeous, turning it mostly green like some kind of forest sprite. I love the shadows on the neck. Just... interesting and weird. I love it!', '2002-12-12 23:38:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(171522, 9463, 1037, '<td valign="top">The composition of this is pretty good, although the colours seem a little bit washed out. I like the DOF you used, bringing the eye right to the stem area of that front lemon. Thematically, though, it''s a bit dull.</td>', 'The composition of this is pretty good, although the colours seem a little bit washed out. I like the DOF you used, bringing the eye right to the stem area of that front lemon. Thematically, though, it''s a bit dull.', '2002-12-12 23:44:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(171524, 9491, 1847, '<td valign="top">The colorized look is very interesting.  Can''t wait to hear how you did it.  Neat pose, too!</td>', 'The colorized look is very interesting.  Can''t wait to hear how you did it.  Neat pose, too!', '2002-12-12 23:44:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(171525, 9553, 1847, '<td valign="top">LOVE the negative space entries.  This one was particularly hard, I bet, cause of how easy it would be to overexpose the foil.  Good job!</td>', 'LOVE the negative space entries.  This one was particularly hard, I bet, cause of how easy it would be to overexpose the foil.  Good job!', '2002-12-12 23:46:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(171526, 9546, 1847, '<td valign="top">Very moody.  Sky looks almost rendered.  All that''s missing is a crow sitting on a branch!</td>', 'Very moody.  Sky looks almost rendered.  All that''s missing is a crow sitting on a branch!', '2002-12-12 23:46:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(171529, 9433, 1847, '<td valign="top">Love lighthouse pics.  Can''t wait to see where this one was taken.  The sky is so pretty and so blue, I''d almost like to see a bit more of it in this photo.</td>', 'Love lighthouse pics.  Can''t wait to see where this one was taken.  The sky is so pretty and so blue, I''d almost like to see a bit more of it in this photo.', '2002-12-12 23:47:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(171530, 9383, 1847, '<td valign="top">Neat perspective.  I''m a HUGE fan of shallow DOF (just check my previous entries!), but I wish it had been just a BIT wider here.</td>', 'Neat perspective.  I''m a HUGE fan of shallow DOF (just check my previous entries!), but I wish it had been just a BIT wider here.', '2002-12-12 23:48:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(171542, 9315, 1037, '<td valign="top">Beautiful! I love the shapes of those flowers. The light is lovely and soft, and the blaick and white adds richness to the broad leaves under the flowers. The only thing that doesn''t seem to work for me is the slightly boxy composition. All those flowers compete to be the centre of attention, and lead my eyes around and around. It might have been better to frame around one or two flowers than the four of them in this group.</td>', 'Beautiful! I love the shapes of those flowers. The light is lovely and soft, and the blaick and white adds richness to the broad leaves under the flowers. The only thing that doesn''t seem to work for me is the slightly boxy composition. All those flowers compete to be the centre of attention, and lead my eyes around and around. It might have been better to frame around one or two flowers than the four of them in this group.', '2002-12-13 00:00:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(171545, 9552, 1037, '<td valign="top">I love it! Great colours and textures here. The water juxtaposes against the grime and decay really beautifully. The composition is spot on, and the light is soft enough to make that blue glaze on the pottery almost glow. Very nice work.</td>', 'I love it! Great colours and textures here. The water juxtaposes against the grime and decay really beautifully. The composition is spot on, and the light is soft enough to make that blue glaze on the pottery almost glow. Very nice work.', '2002-12-13 00:02:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(171548, 9313, 1037, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea. I like the fact that you used a square crop. I can''t really find anything to critique about this photo technically, but thematically it isn''t interesting to me at all. Worth a high mark objectively, but it doesn''t grab me on an emotional level.</td>', 'Interesting idea. I like the fact that you used a square crop. I can''t really find anything to critique about this photo technically, but thematically it isn''t interesting to me at all. Worth a high mark objectively, but it doesn''t grab me on an emotional level.', '2002-12-13 00:05:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(171550, 9585, 1037, '<td valign="top">Nice portrait. I like the shadows on the bridge of her nose, especially. I get a feeling of this woman''s personality, rather than just being presented with a pretty face to look at.<br/> <br/>Whoever took the photo of the girl looking up, lit from below (I forget the title right now), should have a look at what you did here with negative space. You''ve left some empty space in the area of the photo that her eyes lead the viewer towards. This is a good technique, because it makes me wonder what she''s looking at. That goes a long way to creating that feeling of personality and a level of intimacy with the subject of the photo that a tighter crop wouldn''t have given me.</td>', 'Nice portrait. I like the shadows on the bridge of her nose, especially. I get a feeling of this woman''s personality, rather than just being presented with a pretty face to look at. Whoever took the photo of the girl looking up, lit from below (I forget the title right now), should have a look at what you did here with negative space. You''ve left some empty space in the area of the photo that her eyes lead the viewer towards. This is a good technique, because it makes me wonder what she''s looking at. That goes a long way to creating that feeling of personality and a level of intimacy with the subject of the photo that a tighter crop wouldn''t have given me.', '2002-12-13 00:09:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(171554, 9379, 1037, '<td valign="top">This photo serves its purpose well. The composition is formal, but dynamic enough to imply some emotion. I''m sure a lot of people are commenting on the bottom of the wreath being cut off. I really do like the way you framed this, though... a little bit more on the bottom wouldn''t have hurt, but I like the strong shapes. The reflections on the memorial are nice. It''s a good photo, even if I''m a bit disconnected from it emotionally since I''m not an American (although my grandfather fought in Korea).</td>', 'This photo serves its purpose well. The composition is formal, but dynamic enough to imply some emotion. I''m sure a lot of people are commenting on the bottom of the wreath being cut off. I really do like the way you framed this, though... a little bit more on the bottom wouldn''t have hurt, but I like the strong shapes. The reflections on the memorial are nice. It''s a good photo, even if I''m a bit disconnected from it emotionally since I''m not an American (although my grandfather fought in Korea).', '2002-12-13 00:16:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(171557, 9298, 1037, '<td valign="top">The clouds and colours here are nice, but it needs post processing work on levels, curves etc. to really bring out the full range of tones. As it is, it''s washed out and grey. The framing of the tower on the left is awkward, it either needs more of it there or to be cut out completely. The focus is soft, but that''s not a bad thing when the subject is clouds. If it wasn''t so washed out, the soft focus would work well (in my opinion).</td>', 'The clouds and colours here are nice, but it needs post processing work on levels, curves etc. to really bring out the full range of tones. As it is, it''s washed out and grey. The framing of the tower on the left is awkward, it either needs more of it there or to be cut out completely. The focus is soft, but that''s not a bad thing when the subject is clouds. If it wasn''t so washed out, the soft focus would work well (in my opinion).', '2002-12-13 00:19:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(171559, 9491, 1037, '<td valign="top">Technically a great achievement. The colours are lovely, heading towards a kind of sepia toned theme but set off by the flowers. The lighing is lovely and soft, and I really like the way you made her hair kind of unruly, and captured a smile that looks mostly real, not faked for the camera. It''s not really my type of photo, but it looks good enough to be in a calendar  :).</td>', 'Technically a great achievement. The colours are lovely, heading towards a kind of sepia toned theme but set off by the flowers. The lighing is lovely and soft, and I really like the way you made her hair kind of unruly, and captured a smile that looks mostly real, not faked for the camera. It''s not really my type of photo, but it looks good enough to be in a calendar  :).', '2002-12-13 00:24:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(171560, 9367, 1037, '<td valign="top">Interesting geometric study. The lighting is very nice on those white girders. The strands of green stuff make me feel like I''m trapped in a net or something! Very dramatic composition, and overall and effective photo.</td>', 'Interesting geometric study. The lighting is very nice on those white girders. The strands of green stuff make me feel like I''m trapped in a net or something! Very dramatic composition, and overall and effective photo.', '2002-12-13 00:26:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(171561, 9519, 1037, '<td valign="top">Interesting candid... but this is exactly the kind of photo that benefits the most from the rule of thirds. Placing his body further to the left and down a little would mean the direction of his gaze would lead you across the photo to look at the people passing him by, not looking at him, then down to his drums and back around, up to his face. Some work on the colours would also help, they seem a touch washed out (just increase the contrast or work on the levels). Although there is some intest in the left side of the photo because of the bridge, it''s not really adding to the composition at all.</td>', 'Interesting candid... but this is exactly the kind of photo that benefits the most from the rule of thirds. Placing his body further to the left and down a little would mean the direction of his gaze would lead you across the photo to look at the people passing him by, not looking at him, then down to his drums and back around, up to his face. Some work on the colours would also help, they seem a touch washed out (just increase the contrast or work on the levels). Although there is some intest in the left side of the photo because of the bridge, it''s not really adding to the composition at all.', '2002-12-13 00:31:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(171562, 9538, 1037, '<td valign="top">Wow, this photo is just perfect. The black and white is very rich, the metallic sheen is beautiful, but the light is gentle enough to show us every detail. The framing is great, the lines are dynamic but nothing leads the viewer''s eye out of the photo, everything brings it back in. There is enough going on to be interesting, but not confusing. Even though it''s just a set up photo of an inanimate object, it has reached the level of an artwork, transcending  the representational nature of photography. Definitely a 10.</td>', 'Wow, this photo is just perfect. The black and white is very rich, the metallic sheen is beautiful, but the light is gentle enough to show us every detail. The framing is great, the lines are dynamic but nothing leads the viewer''s eye out of the photo, everything brings it back in. There is enough going on to be interesting, but not confusing. Even though it''s just a set up photo of an inanimate object, it has reached the level of an artwork, transcending  the representational nature of photography. Definitely a 10.', '2002-12-13 00:35:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(171563, 9546, 1037, '<td valign="top">Cool... I like the way the completely black forms silhouette starkly against the soft, undulating grey sky. The atmosphere of the photo definitely supports your title. The overall scene is unwelcoming and bleak, and the branches on that tree look gnarled and hostile. Nice work!</td>', 'Cool... I like the way the completely black forms silhouette starkly against the soft, undulating grey sky. The atmosphere of the photo definitely supports your title. The overall scene is unwelcoming and bleak, and the branches on that tree look gnarled and hostile. Nice work!', '2002-12-13 00:38:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(171565, 9345, 1037, '<td valign="top">Wow! Amazing colours and textures here! The composition is really tight. The slightly shallow DOF gives the photo that added dimension of depth. I love that the light is soft enough to bring out every detail. All that rust and erosion is very tactile... I can imagine what it would feel like if I touched it. Looking at this is a blissful experience :). 10!</td>', 'Wow! Amazing colours and textures here! The composition is really tight. The slightly shallow DOF gives the photo that added dimension of depth. I love that the light is soft enough to bring out every detail. All that rust and erosion is very tactile... I can imagine what it would feel like if I touched it. Looking at this is a blissful experience :). 10!', '2002-12-13 00:41:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(171566, 9566, 1037, '<td valign="top">I love it! You caught this woman in such a strong expression and a dynamic pose. It''s really well framed to bring your eye right up to her face. The photo seems a touch oversharpened, or maybe you did some noise removal on it, but that''s only a minor flaw. It''s loaded with personality, and I like that.</td>', 'I love it! You caught this woman in such a strong expression and a dynamic pose. It''s really well framed to bring your eye right up to her face. The photo seems a touch oversharpened, or maybe you did some noise removal on it, but that''s only a minor flaw. It''s loaded with personality, and I like that.', '2002-12-13 00:43:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(171568, 9578, 1037, '<td valign="top">Stunning! The person who took that other icy twig photo in this challenge would do well to compare it to yours. The composition here is beautiful, the DOF brings all the focus onto the front twig and leaf, but there is a dynamic, colourful background to support it. The curl of the leaf is a beautiful shape, and the colour definitely "pops". I love being able to see all the cracks in the ice. This just isn''t a sight I ever see in Australia, so it''s almost alien to me. 10.</td>', 'Stunning! The person who took that other icy twig photo in this challenge would do well to compare it to yours. The composition here is beautiful, the DOF brings all the focus onto the front twig and leaf, but there is a dynamic, colourful background to support it. The curl of the leaf is a beautiful shape, and the colour definitely "pops". I love being able to see all the cracks in the ice. This just isn''t a sight I ever see in Australia, so it''s almost alien to me. 10.', '2002-12-13 00:47:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(171569, 9553, 1037, '<td valign="top">A bold experiment, but the object just isn''t interesting enough, thematically or aesthetically, to make any use of all that space. The fact that the white of the "KISSES" tag blends with the background makes it confusing as well.</td>', 'A bold experiment, but the object just isn''t interesting enough, thematically or aesthetically, to make any use of all that space. The fact that the white of the "KISSES" tag blends with the background makes it confusing as well.', '2002-12-13 00:48:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(171570, 9506, 1037, '<td valign="top">Wow, such rich tones! Something about it just doesn''t sit right with me though. I think you''ve tried to include too much in the photo. A tighter crop around the tree would be very effective, I think. I know that sounds like a very predictable suggestion, but it''s what my instinct tells me, not just to make it conform to the usual standards people apply to photos here :). I still rate it pretty highly though, for its colours and light. It''s a beautiful shot.</td>', 'Wow, such rich tones! Something about it just doesn''t sit right with me though. I think you''ve tried to include too much in the photo. A tighter crop around the tree would be very effective, I think. I know that sounds like a very predictable suggestion, but it''s what my instinct tells me, not just to make it conform to the usual standards people apply to photos here :). I still rate it pretty highly though, for its colours and light. It''s a beautiful shot.', '2002-12-13 00:51:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(171572, 9450, 1037, '<td valign="top">I love your choice of camera angle. The photo doesn''t grab me, but I appreciate the thought you put into it. Many people would benefit from considering angles and composition this way. I can imagine this on the cover of a book.</td>', 'I love your choice of camera angle. The photo doesn''t grab me, but I appreciate the thought you put into it. Many people would benefit from considering angles and composition this way. I can imagine this on the cover of a book.', '2002-12-13 00:56:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(171573, 9452, 1037, '<td valign="top">The photo doesn''t grab me, but I like your lighting. It brings out some nice, soft highlights on the bottle. I just think the still life is a bit bare, the elements don''t connect or support each other particularly well, and the reflections just add to the feeling of disjointedness. The background is nice in an elegant way.</td>', 'The photo doesn''t grab me, but I like your lighting. It brings out some nice, soft highlights on the bottle. I just think the still life is a bit bare, the elements don''t connect or support each other particularly well, and the reflections just add to the feeling of disjointedness. The background is nice in an elegant way.', '2002-12-13 00:58:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(171575, 9561, 1037, '<td valign="top">Very pretty. As abstract photos of inanimate objects go, this one pushes all the right buttons. The colours and tones are rich, the lighting is just right, and the arrangement of the little balls is interesting enough to keep my eyes wandering around for a while. It''s not a really exciting photo, but it''s techically good and I think you achieved what you set out to do.</td>', 'Very pretty. As abstract photos of inanimate objects go, this one pushes all the right buttons. The colours and tones are rich, the lighting is just right, and the arrangement of the little balls is interesting enough to keep my eyes wandering around for a while. It''s not a really exciting photo, but it''s techically good and I think you achieved what you set out to do.', '2002-12-13 01:00:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(171576, 9551, 1037, '<td valign="top">Very cool idea. I love the textures and shapes in this. Your camera angle is great, lifiting the photo and giving us converging lines to draw the viewers eye around. The colours seem a little bit washed out on my monitor, but that''s the only flaw.</td>', 'Very cool idea. I love the textures and shapes in this. Your camera angle is great, lifiting the photo and giving us converging lines to draw the viewers eye around. The colours seem a little bit washed out on my monitor, but that''s the only flaw.', '2002-12-13 01:03:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(171577, 9510, 1037, '<td valign="top">I love the expression you caught! Very spontaneous, and full of personality. The photo is sharp, beautifully exposed and lit with soft, diffuse light. The DOF is great. You''ve pushed all the right buttons, so although the photo doesn''t really grab me I still think it''s objectively worth a high mark.</td>', 'I love the expression you caught! Very spontaneous, and full of personality. The photo is sharp, beautifully exposed and lit with soft, diffuse light. The DOF is great. You''ve pushed all the right buttons, so although the photo doesn''t really grab me I still think it''s objectively worth a high mark.', '2002-12-13 01:06:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(171578, 9473, 1037, '<td valign="top">Hmmm... nice colours, lovely soft  textures, and a nice interplay of light and shade. Although there isn''t really a subject to this photo, it''s kind of nice in an atmospheric, aesthetic and tactile way. Interesting idea.</td>', 'Hmmm... nice colours, lovely soft  textures, and a nice interplay of light and shade. Although there isn''t really a subject to this photo, it''s kind of nice in an atmospheric, aesthetic and tactile way. Interesting idea.', '2002-12-13 01:07:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(171579, 9575, 1037, '<td valign="top">Wow! Your decision to make this quite small actually works for me, although I''m sure you''re getting a lot of complaints. On my monitor, that fork is about 1:1, ie. the size of a real fork. This makes me appreciate how small the snail is. The composition is really tight, the wonderful S curve of the fork and snail just makes me go all gooey :). I love the rich colour of your background, it really sets off the snail.<br/> <br/>Great photo!</td>', 'Wow! Your decision to make this quite small actually works for me, although I''m sure you''re getting a lot of complaints. On my monitor, that fork is about 1:1, ie. the size of a real fork. This makes me appreciate how small the snail is. The composition is really tight, the wonderful S curve of the fork and snail just makes me go all gooey :). I love the rich colour of your background, it really sets off the snail. Great photo!', '2002-12-13 01:09:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(171580, 9559, 1037, '<td valign="top">It seems like your camera is a bit low end and you did some despeckle on it. I don''t mind that, it creates a kind of watercolour effect that I like :). The composition of this photo is spot on, in my opinion. I can''t get enough of rusty girders and bits of old machinery, as long as they''re arranged in an interesting way. The bird is a great touch... juxtaposing nature against artifice. I like it :). Lots of flair, even if the photo is technically flawed.</td>', 'It seems like your camera is a bit low end and you did some despeckle on it. I don''t mind that, it creates a kind of watercolour effect that I like :). The composition of this photo is spot on, in my opinion. I can''t get enough of rusty girders and bits of old machinery, as long as they''re arranged in an interesting way. The bird is a great touch... juxtaposing nature against artifice. I like it :). Lots of flair, even if the photo is technically flawed.', '2002-12-13 01:12:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(171582, 9497, 1037, '<td valign="top">Seems a bit low res, but other than that the DOF is nice and the framing is great. The colours seem a bit muddy, but boosting them would only increase the noise. Maybe it would be nice in black and white?<br/> <br/>Updated to say: This is what I got when I converted it to black and white out of curiosity: //lisa3d.org/images/photos/dpc/birdBW.jpg. I also adjusted the levels, and did a little trick of duplicating a layer, blurring it, turning down the opacity to about 50%, and flattening the photo again. Then I sharpened it a bit. It made it a little less pixellated.</td>', 'Seems a bit low res, but other than that the DOF is nice and the framing is great. The colours seem a bit muddy, but boosting them would only increase the noise. Maybe it would be nice in black and white? Updated to say: This is what I got when I converted it to black and white out of curiosity: //lisa3d.org/images/photos/dpc/birdBW.jpg. I also adjusted the levels, and did a little trick of duplicating a layer, blurring it, turning down the opacity to about 50%, and flattening the photo again. Then I sharpened it a bit. It made it a little less pixellated.', '2002-12-13 01:21:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(171583, 9567, 1037, '<td valign="top">This is a beautiful, serene photo, but I think it could have done with a bit of post-processing work on the colours and levels. The area of sky at the top is a dirty brown colour (at least on my monitor), which could have been altered slightly to bring out the reds and oranges in the sunrise better. I like the silhouette of the trees and the very subtle details I can see of the landscape. The wispy clouds around the sun are gorgeous. Overall, nice work.<br/> <br/>Updated to say: This is what I got when I tried out the suggestions I made: //lisa3d.org/images/photos/dpc/sunrise2.jpg</td>', 'This is a beautiful, serene photo, but I think it could have done with a bit of post-processing work on the colours and levels. The area of sky at the top is a dirty brown colour (at least on my monitor), which could have been altered slightly to bring out the reds and oranges in the sunrise better. I like the silhouette of the trees and the very subtle details I can see of the landscape. The wispy clouds around the sun are gorgeous. Overall, nice work. Updated to say: This is what I got when I tried out the suggestions I made: //lisa3d.org/images/photos/dpc/sunrise2.jpg', '2002-12-13 01:23:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(171650, 9552, 1826, '<td valign="top">Great color, composition. great work.</td>', 'Great color, composition. great work.', '2002-12-13 06:39:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(171651, 9417, 1826, '<td valign="top">Beautiful pet portrait, you didn''t need the border. :) Really like the choice of backround too.</td>', 'Beautiful pet portrait, you didn''t need the border. :) Really like the choice of backround too.', '2002-12-13 06:42:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(171664, 9543, 1202, '<td valign="top">To me this is an inspiring shot.  You have done a wonderful job of presenting your skills.   Would work well in this weeks challenge also.</td>', 'To me this is an inspiring shot.  You have done a wonderful job of presenting your skills.   Would work well in this weeks challenge also.', '2002-12-13 10:11:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(171666, 9578, 1202, '<td valign="top">This is one of only two tens for me this week.   It has everything a DPC photo needs.</td>', 'This is one of only two tens for me this week.   It has everything a DPC photo needs.', '2002-12-13 10:13:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(171667, 9491, 1202, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot and composition.   I feel that is is just a tad light in the facial area.   Great model.</td>', 'Wonderful shot and composition.   I feel that is is just a tad light in the facial area.   Great model.', '2002-12-13 10:15:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(171670, 9575, 1202, '<td valign="top">I feel that you needed to bring out the detail under the snail, and why not make it as big as DPC allows.   It seems subdued due to its small size.</td>', 'I feel that you needed to bring out the detail under the snail, and why not make it as big as DPC allows.   It seems subdued due to its small size.', '2002-12-13 10:18:33.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(171671, 9550, 1202, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting shot, but I think it needs a little more detail on the lower right side, and maybe just a square crop.</td>', 'This is an interesting shot, but I think it needs a little more detail on the lower right side, and maybe just a square crop.', '2002-12-13 10:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(171673, 9538, 1202, '<td valign="top">This is one of my top picks this week.   You did a wonderful job in B/W.</td>', 'This is one of my top picks this week.   You did a wonderful job in B/W.', '2002-12-13 10:26:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(171678, 9383, 2302, '<td valign="top">I like the different colors reflected in the instrument and like the use of the small DOF. The subject matter doesn''t hold my interest for very long though. I would have liked a bit more light on the mouthpiece.  = 6</td>', 'I like the different colors reflected in the instrument and like the use of the small DOF. The subject matter doesn''t hold my interest for very long though. I would have liked a bit more light on the mouthpiece.  = 6', '2002-12-13 10:42:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(171683, 9496, 2302, '<td valign="top">Pretty good details here - you can see the patterns on the bark within the leaves. The colors are a bit drab though. I am not sure if some adjustments would have helped or hurt. I like the composition. The subject matter is ok - made me smile, but doesn''t hold my interest very long. = 6</td>', 'Pretty good details here - you can see the patterns on the bark within the leaves. The colors are a bit drab though. I am not sure if some adjustments would have helped or hurt. I like the composition. The subject matter is ok - made me smile, but doesn''t hold my interest very long. = 6', '2002-12-13 10:45:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(171685, 9459, 2302, '<td valign="top">Fun - I wish I was joining them.  I like how the framing of this picture gives the sense of moving downhill. This is an nice family shot that is different from many you usually see. = 7</td>', 'Fun - I wish I was joining them.  I like how the framing of this picture gives the sense of moving downhill. This is an nice family shot that is different from many you usually see. = 7', '2002-12-13 10:49:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(171686, 9378, 2302, '<td valign="top">Nice composition here. The lighting seems a bit off to me - too much on the left side and not quite enough on the right. Nice details, Nice colors. = 6</td>', 'Nice composition here. The lighting seems a bit off to me - too much on the left side and not quite enough on the right. Nice details, Nice colors. = 6', '2002-12-13 10:51:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(171687, 9345, 2302, '<td valign="top">Nice colors and textures here. The white border is a bit harsh, I might have tried something a little less bright for this picture. Good capture of details and nice composition. = 8</td>', 'Nice colors and textures here. The white border is a bit harsh, I might have tried something a little less bright for this picture. Good capture of details and nice composition. = 8', '2002-12-13 10:54:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(171688, 9519, 2302, '<td valign="top">Looks scary. Nice focus, nice details and composition. Overall this doesn''t have a lot of interest for me. = 7</td>', 'Looks scary. Nice focus, nice details and composition. Overall this doesn''t have a lot of interest for me. = 7', '2002-12-13 10:56:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(171694, 9378, 3706, '<td valign="top">I love this shot.... very soothing. :)</td>', 'I love this shot.... very soothing. :)', '2002-12-13 11:07:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(171698, 9550, 2000, '<td valign="top">Creative capture - I like the level of detail, as you can see each seed distinctly with good colors.</td>', 'Creative capture - I like the level of detail, as you can see each seed distinctly with good colors.', '2002-12-13 11:13:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(171702, 9402, 2553, '<td valign="top">A unique idea with a good composition.  I am not particularly crazy about this photo however, mostly, I think, because of the greenish-yellow cast on the skin on the left side.  I think that I would have preferred to see a warmer (maybe red-orange) color on the majority skin - sort of what I am seeing on the right.  lhall 8</td>', 'A unique idea with a good composition.  I am not particularly crazy about this photo however, mostly, I think, because of the greenish-yellow cast on the skin on the left side.  I think that I would have preferred to see a warmer (maybe red-orange) color on the majority skin - sort of what I am seeing on the right.  lhall 8', '2002-12-13 11:37:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(171705, 9388, 772, '<td valign="top">excellent macro... the detail and depth of field are quite nice here :) - setzler</td>', 'excellent macro... the detail and depth of field are quite nice here :) - setzler', '2002-12-13 11:40:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(171706, 9526, 2553, '<td valign="top">Nice clear shot, with fairly good composition, I think I would have liked to have seen it cropped in about an inch or so on the right hand side.  Not high impact for me, possibly because I have no real interest in canoes!  However, I do like the colors, and the juxtaposition of old against new.  Overall a nice shot.  lhall 7</td>', 'Nice clear shot, with fairly good composition, I think I would have liked to have seen it cropped in about an inch or so on the right hand side.  Not high impact for me, possibly because I have no real interest in canoes!  However, I do like the colors, and the juxtaposition of old against new.  Overall a nice shot.  lhall 7', '2002-12-13 11:42:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(171707, 9367, 2553, '<td valign="top">I like your composition and the repeating of lines and angles - makes it a very interesting shot.  I also like the limited color palette. Wonderful imagination to choose this angle and composition!  lhall</td>', 'I like your composition and the repeating of lines and angles - makes it a very interesting shot.  I also like the limited color palette. Wonderful imagination to choose this angle and composition!  lhall', '2002-12-13 11:44:08.000000', NULL, 1),
