(173282, 9582, 3018, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for your comments.  Now to explain a little on how I got the effect for the ball and the white background: I used the Levels tool in Photoshop to get that pure white background.  I have to use this tool, because I don''t have proper lighting.  I used normal light bulbs for this picture, so those caused the background to have a horrible dirty yellow color, and it also turned my xmas red ball into an orange ball.  What I did like is that after I used the Levels tool to get the white color, the ball seemed a little bit two dimensional, so the picture now looked like a xmas card.  After that, I only had to crop the picture and applied some sharpening.  Thanks for you compliments and also the tips for how to improve my picture, specially about the out of focus branch.</td>', 'Thanks everyone for your comments.  Now to explain a little on how I got the effect for the ball and the white background: I used the Levels tool in Photoshop to get that pure white background.  I have to use this tool, because I don''t have proper lighting.  I used normal light bulbs for this picture, so those caused the background to have a horrible dirty yellow color, and it also turned my xmas red ball into an orange ball.  What I did like is that after I used the Levels tool to get the white color, the ball seemed a little bit two dimensional, so the picture now looked like a xmas card.  After that, I only had to crop the picture and applied some sharpening.  Thanks for you compliments and also the tips for how to improve my picture, specially about the out of focus branch.', '2002-12-16 11:29:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(173323, 9336, 1037, '<td valign="top">Wow, I''m the only person who gave this a 10!</td>', 'Wow, I''m the only person who gave this a 10!', '2002-12-16 12:36:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(173414, 9340, 4852, '<td valign="top">This is not pudding or a tub of butter. Its a piece of plastic I molded to a bowl shape . I was attempting to use it for the motion challenge by spinning marbles around in it while using a strobe light. I didnt like the results. So I shot this and others with stationary marbles. The yellow cast is from setting the incorrect white balance.<a href="//www.pbase.com/badpigg/inbox" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">other examples</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2002-12-16 14:18:39.</i></td>', 'This is not pudding or a tub of butter. Its a piece of plastic I molded to a bowl shape . I was attempting to use it for the motion challenge by spinning marbles around in it while using a strobe light. I didnt like the results. So I shot this and others with stationary marbles. The yellow cast is from setting the incorrect white balance.other examples', '2002-12-16 13:54:01.000000', '2002-12-16 14:18:39.000000', 0),
(173644, 9578, 1005, '<td valign="top">Look at that!  No 1s, 2s or 3s!  And only one 4.  This was my favorite for the week.  Great eye!  The crackled ice really puts this one into a class by itself.  Wonderful!  (easy fav!)</td>', 'Look at that!  No 1s, 2s or 3s!  And only one 4.  This was my favorite for the week.  Great eye!  The crackled ice really puts this one into a class by itself.  Wonderful!  (easy fav!)', '2002-12-16 16:50:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(173651, 9482, 1005, '<td valign="top">Look at that score breakdown!  I''ve never seen such a lack of low numbers!  Well deserved score!  Lots of WOW factor in this one.</td>', 'Look at that score breakdown!  I''ve never seen such a lack of low numbers!  Well deserved score!  Lots of WOW factor in this one.', '2002-12-16 16:53:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(173686, 9417, 327, '<td valign="top">Critique Club #15<br/>Composition: This is a fine shot of a great looking dog. Hard not to like him. The dog is centered and ''in your face''. In this case I think it works very well. Usually the lone subject centered is not as appealing. The expression, eyes ...=LOVE. I think the top could of been cropped just a bit, too much dead space.<br/>Background: White. I think it works very well here. The frame matches the collar and draws the eye to the dogs neck. <br/>Camera Work/Technical:Very nice. I would only suggest that the cameara been a bit lower-maybe eye level. The shot is sharp, crisp, in focus and has good lighting.<br/>My Opinion: A very good shot. It''s a perfect animal, showing love.</td>', 'Critique Club #15Composition: This is a fine shot of a great looking dog. Hard not to like him. The dog is centered and ''in your face''. In this case I think it works very well. Usually the lone subject centered is not as appealing. The expression, eyes ...=LOVE. I think the top could of been cropped just a bit, too much dead space.Background: White. I think it works very well here. The frame matches the collar and draws the eye to the dogs neck. Camera Work/Technical:Very nice. I would only suggest that the cameara been a bit lower-maybe eye level. The shot is sharp, crisp, in focus and has good lighting.My Opinion: A very good shot. It''s a perfect animal, showing love.', '2002-12-16 17:13:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(173693, 9497, 327, '<td valign="top">Critique Club # 47<br/>Composition-Content:  This is good capture of a nice looking, colorful bird.<br/>The Finch is the main focus of the shot.<br/>I''m not crazy about the little branch nub on the lower edge right.<br/>Background:  The colors are very nice.<br/>Camera Work-Technical:  Exposure and light are good, but the focus is soft. I''m sure it''s due to<br/>the window glass. I''m not sure if a tripod was used here, but if not it''s a steady hand.<br/>My opinion:  Good capture and good color. Of course better focus would of helped this shot, but over all<br/>it''s very nice.<br/></td>', 'Critique Club # 47Composition-Content:  This is good capture of a nice looking, colorful bird.The Finch is the main focus of the shot.I''m not crazy about the little branch nub on the lower edge right.Background:  The colors are very nice.Camera Work-Technical:  Exposure and light are good, but the focus is soft. I''m sure it''s due tothe window glass. I''m not sure if a tripod was used here, but if not it''s a steady hand.My opinion:  Good capture and good color. Of course better focus would of helped this shot, but over allit''s very nice.', '2002-12-16 17:20:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(173722, 9494, 3080, '<td valign="top">I''m shocked that so many people wanted the color here.  I think that with the color, this would be horribly cluttered.  There would be too much to look at.  Having it in black and white lets us look at what is really interesting, the shapes.  Anyway, I was the one that gave you the 9. I thought you did a nice job with this.  Aside from the bright shirt, it''s a great shot.</td>', 'I''m shocked that so many people wanted the color here.  I think that with the color, this would be horribly cluttered.  There would be too much to look at.  Having it in black and white lets us look at what is really interesting, the shapes.  Anyway, I was the one that gave you the 9. I thought you did a nice job with this.  Aside from the bright shirt, it''s a great shot.', '2002-12-16 17:52:48.000000', NULL, 0),
